<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Thuwayni ibn Abdullah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. 1797</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Thuwayni ibn Abdullah (died 1797) was a sheikh of the Al Saadun, the ruling family of the Muntafiq tribal confederation of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a>. He seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/basra">Basra</a> from the Ottoman authorities in 1787 but was driven out by forces sent from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a>. Later restored to favour, he was killed in 1797 while leading an Ottoman-backed campaign against the Wahhabis.</p></div>
